On 08/14/2015 08:54 AM, Gleki Arxokuna wrote:
>
>
> 2015-08-14 15:04 GMT+03:00 Ilmen <ilmen.pokebip@gmail.com 
> <mailto:ilmen.pokebip@gmail.com>>:
>
>     coi lo ro do
>
>     *CLL 1.0 Chapter 6:
>     *
>     15.3)  li .abu bopi'i xy. bote'a re su'i by. bopi'i xy. su'i cy.
>            the-number a times x to-power 2 plus b times x plus c
>            ax^2   + bx + c
>
>     It's the first time ever I see this bo+VUhU pattern, and it seems
>     this example sentence from the CLL is not grammatical under any of
>     the following parsers: YACC, Jbofihe, Visual Camxes, Camxes JS.
>
>
> Neither  do formal grammars of CLL where the only mentions of them in 
> mekso are
> https://lojban.github.io/cll/21/1/#y915
> https://lojban.github.io/cll/21/1/#y1010
> https://lojban.github.io/cll/21/1/#y1005
>

I'm convinced this is a CLL error. It looks like the intent is to get 
right-associativity, so that the ^2 affects "x", and so "x^2" is in turn 
multiplied by "a". In the second term, the "bo" is used particularly for 
tight binding, to prevent the default equal left-association of all 
VUhU. These BO+VUhU should all be VUhU+BO.

.i mi'e la tsani mu'o

